# TWC Mission Server Cline Rules

Before doing anything, CAREFULLY check whether you are in ACT MODE that allows editing and writing to files or some other mode (such as PLAN MODE or ARCHITECT MODE) that does not allow file writing or changes. UNLESS YOU ARE IN ACT MODE, do not try to write or change files in any way. 

- If you are in PLAN or ARCHITECT mode: Simply inform the user of the plan, in detail, in the chat. Create and present a plan that can be implemented by a different, less intelligent worker.

- If you are in ACT MODE: Follow the test plan exactly, step by step, with no deviation.  If problems arise or changes to the plan seem necessary, stop and ask the user how to proceed.  Do not make any changes to the plan without asking first. Before beginning, write the plan to a file in the genghis directory called plan-[date-time].md so that we can continue if interrupted. As you work through this plan step by step, mark each completed step with "[COMPLETED-date-time]".

- This repo holds several INDEPENDENT campaigns/projects, one per subdirectory: Genghis (the active
   one), Campaign21, M001, M002, M003, Testing, Tobruk_Campaign. They are related in various ways but are
   separate and self-contained - never root around in a sibling campaign (e.g. Campaign21) while working
   on Genghis; its code is a different, older campaign, not the thing being edited.
 - Genghis\ is the actively developed project. Genghis.cs plus the Genghis-Class-*.cs files in that same
   folder are the working set. Ask before touching anything else.
 - Full layout, module map and known pitfalls: see .clinerules-long in this folder.

 - After editing any .cs in Genghis\, verify it compiles:
     pwsh -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Genghis\check-compile.ps1
   Run from TWC_Mission_Server\. Exit 0 = OK, 1 = compile errors, 2 = could not run.
   Baseline: 0 errors, ~64 warnings (suppressed by default; -ShowWarnings to list).
 - MISSION CODE MUST STAY C#5: check-compile.ps1 pins `/langversion:5` to match the CLoD mission
   compiler (C#5-era, runs on the server). C#6/7+ syntax (e.g. pattern matching `x is AiAircraft y`,
   string interpolation `$"..."`, `out var`, `?.`, `nameof`) compiles locally on a modern SDK if you
   edit by hand but the SERVER rejects it at deploy time (CS1026/CS1002/CS1525 or CS8026). Use old
   idioms: `as` + null check, string concatenation, named `out` vars. Genghis.csproj's LangVersion 7.3
   is IDE-only and does NOT apply here.
 - NEVER `dotnet build` the repo TWC_Mission_Server.csproj - it is SDK-style and globs EVERY .cs in the
   tree, including the duplicate mission copies under Campaign21\, Tobruk_Campaign\ and Testing\, which
   redefine Mission / Calcs / CoverCalcs and yield thousands of duplicate-type errors.
 - Genghis\Genghis.csproj is DESIGN-TIME ONLY (IDE IntelliSense, registered in TWC_Mission_Server.sln).
   Not the build truth - use check-compile.ps1 for that. Targets net481 (CloD DLLs built against .NET 4.8.1).
   Two known CS0122 errors in Genghis-Class-TacviewRecorder.cs (TacviewCore internal) are expected.
